{"id":"mahabharata-12-029","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":29,"title":"एकोनत्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 29 · Arjuna asks Krishna; the sixteen kings","summary":{"en":"Arjuna asks Krishna to console the silent Yudhishthira, and Krishna tells him of Narada's account to Srinjaya of sixteen great kings who died and whose glory remains. The tale of Marutta, Suhotra, Shibi and the others shows that even the mighty all pass away.","kn":"ಮೌನ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನನ್ನು ಸಂತೈಸಲು ಅರ್ಜುನ ಕೃಷ್ಣನನ್ನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೃಷ್ಣ ನಾರದ ಸೃಂಜಯನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳಿದ, ಸತ್ತರೂ ಕೀರ್ತಿ ಉಳಿದ ಹದಿನಾರು ಮಹಾರಾಜರ ಕಥೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಮರುತ್ತ, ಸುಹೋತ್ರ, ಶಿಬಿ ಮೊದಲಾದವರ ಕಥೆ ಶಕ್ತಿಶಾಲಿಗಳೂ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾರೆಂದು ತೋರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"अर्जुन कृष्ण से मौन युधिष्ठिर को समझाने को कहते हैं, और कृष्ण नारद द्वारा सृंजय को सुनाई सोलह महान राजाओं की कथा बताते हैं जो मरे पर जिनका यश बना रहा। मरुत्त, सुहोत्र, शिबि आदि की कथा दिखाती है कि बलवान भी चले जाते हैं।","te":"మౌనంగా ఉన్న యుధిష్ఠిరుని ఓదార్చమని అర్జునుడు కృష్ణుని అడుగుతాడు; కృష్ణుడు నారదుడు సృంజయునికి చెప్పిన, మరణించినా కీర్తి నిలిచిన పదహారు మహారాజుల కథ చెబుతాడు. మరుత్తు, సుహోత్రుడు, శిబి మొదలైనవారి కథ బలవంతులూ పోతారని చూపుతుంది.","ta":"மௌனமாக இருக்கும் யுதிஷ்டிரரைத் தேற்றும்படி அர்ஜுனன் கண்ணனைக் கேட்க, இறந்தும் புகழ் நிலைத்த பதினாறு மாமன்னரின் கதையை நாரதர் சிருஞ்சயனுக்குக் கூறியதைக் கண்ணன் சொல்கிறார். மருத்தன், சுஹோத்ரன், சிபி முதலியோரின் கதை வலியோரும் மறைவர் என்று காட்டுகிறது.","ml":"മൗനത്തിലിരിക്കുന്ന യുധിഷ്ഠിരനെ ആശ്വസിപ്പിക്കാൻ അർജുനൻ കൃഷ്ണനോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു; നാരദൻ സൃഞ്ജയനോട് പറഞ്ഞ, മരിച്ചുപോയ പതിനാറു മഹാരാജാക്കളുടെ കഥ കൃഷ്ണൻ പറയുന്നു. മരുത്തൻ, സുഹോത്രൻ, ശിബി തുടങ്ങിയവരുടെ കഥ കാണിക്കുന്നത് എത്ര ശക്തരും മരിച്ചുപോകുമെന്നാണ്; അവരുടെ മഹത്ത്വം മാത്രം ശേഷിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.29; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अव्याहरति कौन्तेये धर्मपुत्रे युधिष्ठिरे ।\nगुडाकेशो हृषीकेशमभ्यभाषत पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Yudhishthira, Kunti's son and the son of Dharma, stayed silent, the Pandava Arjuna, lord of sleep, spoke to Hrishikesha."}},{"n":2,"text":"ज्ञातिशोकाभिसंतप्तो धर्मराजः परंतपः ।\nएष शोकार्णवे मग्नस्तमाश्वासय माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dharmaraja Yudhishthira, scorcher of foes, is tormented by grief for his kinsmen and has sunk into an ocean of sorrow; console him, Madhava."}},{"n":3,"text":"सर्वे स्म ते संशयिताः पुनरेव जनार्दन ।\nअस्य शोकं महाबाहो प्रणाशयितुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Janardana, all of us are again in doubt; mighty-armed one, you alone can remove his grief."}},{"n":4,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु गोविन्दो विजयेन महात्मना ।\nपर्यवर्तत राजानं पुण्डरीकेक्षणोऽच्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to thus by the great-souled Arjuna, Govinda, the lotus-eyed and unfallen, turned toward the king."}},{"n":5,"text":"अनतिक्रमणीयो हि धर्मराजस्य केशवः ।\nबाल्यात्प्रभृति गोविन्दः प्रीत्या चाभ्यधिकोऽर्जुनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For Keshava could not cross Dharmaraja's wishes, and from childhood Govinda loved him even more than Arjuna."}},{"n":6,"text":"संप्रगृह्य महाबाहुर्भुजं चन्दनभूषितम् ।\nशैलस्तम्भोपमं शौरिरुवाचाभिविनोदयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty-armed Shauri took the king's sandal-smeared arm, as firm as a mountain pillar, and spoke to cheer him."}},{"n":7,"text":"शुशुभे वदनं तस्य सुदंष्ट्रं चारुलोचनम् ।\nव्याकोशमिव विस्पष्टं पद्मं सूर्यविबोधितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His face with its fine teeth and lovely eyes shone clearly, like a lotus opened wide by the sun."}},{"n":8,"text":"मा कृथाः पुरुषव्याघ्र शोकं त्वं गात्रशोषणम् ।\nन हि ते सुलभा भूयो ये हतास्मिन्रणाजिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tiger among men, do not give way to grief that wastes the body; those who have fallen on this battlefield are not easy to find again."}},{"n":9,"text":"स्वप्नलब्धा यथा लाभा वितथाः प्रतिबोधने ।\nएवं ते क्षत्रिया राजन्ये व्यतीता महारणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like gains won in a dream that prove false on waking, so those warriors, O king, have passed away in the great war."}},{"n":10,"text":"सर्वे ह्यभिमुखाः शूरा विगता रणशोभिनः ।\nनैषां कश्चित्पृष्ठतो वा पलायन्वापि पातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All those heroes, who adorned the battle, faced the enemy; not one of them was struck down while fleeing or turning his back."}},{"n":11,"text":"सर्वे त्यक्त्वात्मनः प्राणान्युद्ध्वा वीरा महाहवे ।\nशस्त्रपूता दिवं प्राप्ता न ताञ्शोचितुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"All those heroes gave up their lives fighting in the great battle, and purified by weapons they reached heaven; you should not grieve for them."}},{"n":12,"text":"अत्रैवोदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nसृञ्जयं पुत्रशोकार्तं यथायं प्राह नारदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this very point they tell an ancient tale, how Narada once spoke to Srinjaya, who was stricken with grief for his son."}},{"n":13,"text":"सुखदुःखैरहं त्वं च प्रजाः सर्वाश्च सृञ्जय ।\nअविमुक्तं चरिष्यामस्तत्र का परिदेवना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Narada said: Srinjaya, you and I and all creatures move through pleasure and pain without ever being free of them; so what use is lamenting?"}},{"n":14,"text":"महाभाग्यं परं राज्ञां कीर्त्यमानं मया शृणु ।\nगच्छावधानं नृपते ततो दुःखं प्रहास्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen to me recount the supreme greatness of kings; give me your attention, O king, and you will cast off your sorrow."}},{"n":15,"text":"मृतान्महानुभावांस्त्वं श्रुत्वैव तु महीपतीन् ।\nश्रुत्वापनय संतापं शृणु विस्तरशश्च मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing only that these mighty rulers died, put away your torment; listen to me in detail."}},{"n":16,"text":"आविक्षितं मरुत्तं मे मृतं सृञ्जय शुश्रुहि ।\nयस्य सेन्द्राः सवरुणा बृहस्पतिपुरोगमाः ।\nदेवा विश्वसृजो राज्ञो यज्ञमीयुर्महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, hear that Marutta, son of Avikshit, also died; for his sacrifice the gods came, with Indra, Varuna and Brihaspati leading, the makers of the world."}},{"n":17,"text":"यः स्पर्धामनयच्छक्रं देवराजं शतक्रतुम् ।\nशक्रप्रियैषी यं विद्वान्प्रत्याचष्ट बृहस्पतिः ।\nसंवर्तो याजयामास यं पीडार्थं बृहस्पतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was the one who challenged Indra of the hundred sacrifices; wise Brihaspati, wishing to please Indra, refused to officiate for him, and Samvarta performed his rites to spite Brihaspati."}},{"n":18,"text":"यस्मिन्प्रशासति सतां नृपतौ नृपसत्तम ।\nअकृष्टपच्या पृथिवी विबभौ चैत्यमालिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of kings, while that good king ruled, the earth shone with sacred shrines like garlands and bore crops without being ploughed."}},{"n":19,"text":"आविक्षितस्य वै सत्रे विश्वे देवाः सभासदः ।\nमरुतः परिवेष्टारः साध्याश्चासन्महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At Marutta's sacrifice the Vishvedevas were the assembly, the Maruts the servers, and the Sadhyas were there too."}},{"n":20,"text":"मरुद्गणा मरुत्तस्य यत्सोममपिबन्त ते ।\nदेवान्मनुष्यान्गन्धर्वानत्यरिच्यन्त दक्षिणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Marut hosts drank Marutta's soma, and his sacrificial gifts surpassed those given to gods, men and gandharvas."}},{"n":21,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son."}},{"n":22,"text":"सुहोत्रं चेद्वैतिथिनं मृतं सृञ्जय शुश्रुम ।\nयस्मै हिरण्यं ववृषे मघवान्परिवत्सरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that Suhotra, son of Vitithi, also died; for him Indra rained gold for a whole year."}},{"n":23,"text":"सत्यनामा वसुमती यं प्राप्यासीज्जनाधिप ।\nहिरण्यमवहन्नद्यस्तस्मिञ्जनपदेश्वरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of men, the earth became truly worthy of her name, rich in treasure, when she gained him; rivers carried gold in that king's land."}},{"n":24,"text":"कूर्मान्कर्कटकान्नक्रान्मकराञ्शिंशुकानपि ।\nनदीष्वपातयद्राजन्मघवा लोकपूजितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The world-honored Indra dropped into the rivers turtles, crabs, crocodiles, sea monsters and porpoises, all of gold."}},{"n":25,"text":"हैरण्यान्पतितान्दृष्ट्वा मत्स्यान्मकरकच्छपान् ।\nसहस्रशोऽथ शतशस्ततोऽस्मयत वैतिथिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing golden fish, makaras and tortoises fall by the hundreds and thousands, Vaitithi smiled."}},{"n":26,"text":"तद्धिरण्यमपर्यन्तमावृत्तं कुरुजाङ्गले ।\nईजानो वितते यज्ञे ब्राह्मणेभ्यः समाहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At his wide-spread sacrifice he gave away that endless gold, gathered in Kurujangala, with focused mind to the brahmins."}},{"n":27,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ।\nअदक्षिणमयज्वानं श्वैत्य संशाम्य मा शुचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son; calm yourself, Shaibya, and do not mourn one who gave no fees and performed no sacrifice."}},{"n":28,"text":"अङ्गं बृहद्रथं चैव मृतं शुश्रुम सृञ्जय ।\nयः सहस्रं सहस्राणां श्वेतानश्वानवासृजत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that Anga Brihadratha also died, who let loose a thousand times a thousand white horses."}},{"n":29,"text":"सहस्रं च सहस्राणां कन्या हेमविभूषिताः ।\nईजानो वितते यज्ञे दक्षिणामत्यकालयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At his wide-spread sacrifice he drove forth as fees a thousand times a thousand maidens adorned with gold."}},{"n":30,"text":"शतं शतसहस्राणां वृषाणां हेममालिनाम् ।\nगवां सहस्रानुचरं दक्षिणामत्यकालयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He drove forth as fees a hundred times a hundred thousand bulls wearing golden garlands, each with a thousand cows following."}},{"n":31,"text":"अङ्गस्य यजमानस्य तदा विष्णुपदे गिरौ ।\nअमाद्यदिन्द्रः सोमेन दक्षिणाभिर्द्विजातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Anga performed his sacrifice on the Vishnupada mountain, Indra was exhilarated by the soma and the brahmins by the fees."}},{"n":32,"text":"यस्य यज्ञेषु राजेन्द्र शतसंख्येषु वै पुनः ।\nदेवान्मनुष्यान्गन्धर्वानत्यरिच्यन्त दक्षिणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, at his hundred sacrifices the fees surpassed those given to gods, men and gandharvas."}},{"n":33,"text":"न जातो जनिता चान्यः पुमान्यस्तत्प्रदास्यति ।\nयदङ्गः प्रददौ वित्तं सोमसंस्थासु सप्तसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"No other man has been born or will be born who could give what Anga gave at the seven soma sacrifices."}},{"n":34,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son."}},{"n":35,"text":"शिबिमौशीनरं चैव मृतं शुश्रुम सृञ्जय ।\nय इमां पृथिवीं कृत्स्नां चर्मवत्समवेष्टयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that Shibi Aushinara also died, who wrapped up this whole earth like a hide."}},{"n":36,"text":"महता रथघोषेण पृथिवीमनुनादयन् ।\nएकच्छत्रां महीं चक्रे जैत्रेणैकरथेन यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Filling the earth with the great roar of his chariot, he made it one realm under a single umbrella with his single victorious chariot."}},{"n":37,"text":"यावदद्य गवाश्वं स्यादारण्यैः पशुभिः सह ।\nतावतीः प्रददौ गाः स शिबिरौशीनरोऽध्वरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As many cows and horses as exist today together with wild animals, that many cows Shibi Aushinara gave at his sacrifice."}},{"n":38,"text":"नोद्यन्तारं धुरं तस्य कंचिन्मेने प्रजापतिः ।\nन भूतं न भविष्यन्तं सर्वराजसु भारत ।\nअन्यत्रौशीनराच्छैब्याद्राजर्षेरिन्द्रविक्रमात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Creator knew no one, past or future, among all kings who could bear his burden, Bharata, except the royal sage Shibi Aushinara, with Indra's prowess."}},{"n":39,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ।\nअदक्षिणमयज्वानं तं वै संशाम्य मा शुचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son; calm yourself over one who gave no fees and performed no sacrifice."}},{"n":40,"text":"भरतं चैव दौःषन्तिं मृतं सृञ्जय शुश्रुम ।\nशाकुन्तलिं महेष्वासं भूरिद्रविणतेजसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that Bharata, son of Dushyanta and Shakuntala, the great archer of vast wealth and splendor, also died."}},{"n":41,"text":"यो बद्ध्वा त्रिंशतो ह्यश्वान्देवेभ्यो यमुनामनु ।\nसरस्वतीं विंशतिं च गङ्गामनु चतुर्दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"He tied thirty horses for the gods along the Yamuna, twenty along the Sarasvati, and fourteen along the Ganga."}},{"n":42,"text":"अश्वमेधसहस्रेण राजसूयशतेन च ।\nइष्टवान्स महातेजा दौःषन्तिर्भरतः पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the past the radiant Bharata, Dushyanta's son, performed a thousand horse sacrifices and a hundred royal consecrations."}},{"n":43,"text":"भरतस्य महत्कर्म सर्वराजसु पार्थिवाः ।\nखं मर्त्या इव बाहुभ्यां नानुगन्तुमशक्नुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings, mortals could not follow Bharata's great deed among all rulers, as men cannot follow the sky with their arms."}},{"n":44,"text":"परं सहस्राद्यो बद्ध्वा हयान्वेदीं विचित्य च ।\nसहस्रं यत्र पद्मानां कण्वाय भरतो ददौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"He tied up more than a thousand horses and searched out the altar, and there Bharata gave Kanva a thousand padmas."}},{"n":45,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son."}},{"n":46,"text":"रामं दाशरथिं चैव मृतं शुश्रुम सृञ्जय ।\nयोऽन्वकम्पत वै नित्यं प्रजाः पुत्रानिवौरसान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that Rama, son of Dasharatha, also died, who always showed his subjects the kindness he would show his own sons."}},{"n":47,"text":"विधवा यस्य विषये नानाथाः काश्चनाभवन् ।\nसर्वस्यासीत्पितृसमो रामो राज्यं यदान्वशात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In his kingdom no widow lacked a protector; while Rama ruled, he was like a father to all."}},{"n":48,"text":"कालवर्षाश्च पर्जन्याः सस्यानि रसवन्ति च ।\nनित्यं सुभिक्षमेवासीद्रामे राज्यं प्रशासति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rains came in their season, crops were full of sap, and there was always plenty while Rama ruled."}},{"n":49,"text":"प्राणिनो नाप्सु मज्जन्ति नानर्थे पावकोऽदहत् ।\nन व्यालजं भयं चासीद्रामे राज्यं प्रशासति ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Rama ruled, creatures did not drown in water, fire burned only to purpose, and there was no fear from beasts of prey."}},{"n":50,"text":"आसन्वर्षसहस्राणि तथा पुत्रसहस्रिकाः ।\nअरोगाः सर्वसिद्धार्थाः प्रजा रामे प्रशासति ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Rama ruled, subjects lived for thousands of years with thousands of sons, free of disease and with all aims fulfilled."}},{"n":51,"text":"नान्योन्येन विवादोऽभूत्स्त्रीणामपि कुतो नृणाम् ।\nधर्मनित्याः प्रजाश्चासन्रामे राज्यं प्रशासति ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Rama ruled, there was no quarrel among men, let alone among women, and the people were constant in dharma."}},{"n":52,"text":"नित्यपुष्पफलाश्चैव पादपा निरुपद्रवाः ।\nसर्वा द्रोणदुघा गावो रामे राज्यं प्रशासति ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Rama ruled, trees bore flowers and fruit all year without harm, and all cows gave a full measure of milk."}},{"n":53,"text":"स चतुर्दश वर्षाणि वने प्रोष्य महातपाः ।\nदशाश्वमेधाञ्जारूथ्यानाजहार निरर्गलान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great ascetic spent fourteen years in the forest and then performed ten unrestricted horse sacrifices with the closing bath."}},{"n":54,"text":"श्यामो युवा लोहिताक्षो मत्तवारणविक्रमः ।\nदश वर्षसहस्राणि रामो राज्यमकारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dark, young and red-eyed, moving like a rutting elephant, Rama ruled the kingdom for ten thousand years."}},{"n":55,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son."}},{"n":56,"text":"भगीरथं च राजानं मृतं शुश्रुम सृञ्जय ।\nयस्येन्द्रो वितते यज्ञे सोमं पीत्वा मदोत्कटः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that King Bhagiratha also died, at whose wide-spread sacrifice Indra, wild with drinking soma,"}},{"n":57,"text":"असुराणां सहस्राणि बहूनि सुरसत्तमः ।\nअजयद्बाहुवीर्येण भगवान्पाकशासनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the blessed best of gods, punisher of Paka, conquered many thousands of asuras with the strength of his arms."}},{"n":58,"text":"यः सहस्रं सहस्राणां कन्या हेमविभूषिताः ।\nईजानो वितते यज्ञे दक्षिणामत्यकालयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhagiratha gave as fees at his wide-spread sacrifice a thousand times a thousand maidens adorned with gold."}},{"n":59,"text":"सर्वा रथगताः कन्या रथाः सर्वे चतुर्युजः ।\nरथे रथे शतं नागाः पद्मिनो हेममालिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the maidens rode in chariots, all the chariots had four horses, and with each chariot went a hundred elephants wearing lotus garlands and gold."}},{"n":60,"text":"सहस्रमश्वा एकैकं हस्तिनं पृष्ठतोऽन्वयुः ।\nगवां सहस्रमश्वेऽश्वे सहस्रं गव्यजाविकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A thousand horses followed behind each elephant, a thousand cows followed each horse, and a thousand goats and sheep followed each cow."}},{"n":61,"text":"उपह्वरे निवसतो यस्याङ्के निषसाद ह ।\nगङ्गा भागीरथी तस्मादुर्वशी ह्यभवत्पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he lived in his retreat, Ganga, Bhagiratha's daughter, once sat on his lap, and so she became Urvashi in the past."}},{"n":62,"text":"भूरिदक्षिणमिक्ष्वाकुं यजमानं भगीरथम् ।\nत्रिलोकपथगा गङ्गा दुहितृत्वमुपेयुषी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ganga, who travels the three worlds, became the daughter of Bhagiratha, the Ikshvaku who gave rich fees at his sacrifices."}},{"n":63,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son."}},{"n":64,"text":"दिलीपं चैवैलविलं मृतं शुश्रुम सृञ्जय ।\nयस्य कर्माणि भूरीणि कथयन्ति द्विजातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that Dilipa, son of Ila, also died, whose many deeds the brahmins recite."}},{"n":65,"text":"इमां वै वसुसंपन्नां वसुधां वसुधाधिपः ।\nददौ तस्मिन्महायज्ञे ब्राह्मणेभ्यः समाहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That lord of the earth gave this earth, rich in treasure, to the brahmins at his great sacrifice, with focused mind."}},{"n":66,"text":"तस्येह यजमानस्य यज्ञे यज्ञे पुरोहितः ।\nसहस्रं वारणान्हैमान्दक्षिणामत्यकालयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At each sacrifice of that sacrificer, the priest drove away a thousand golden elephants as fees."}},{"n":67,"text":"यस्य यज्ञे महानासीद्यूपः श्रीमान्हिरण्मयः ।\nतं देवाः कर्म कुर्वाणाः शक्रज्येष्ठा उपाश्रयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At his sacrifice the great, splendid golden sacrificial post stood, and the gods, led by Indra, resorted to it as they did their work."}},{"n":68,"text":"चषालो यस्य सौवर्णस्तस्मिन्यूपे हिरण्मये ।\nननृतुर्देवगन्धर्वाः षट्सहस्राणि सप्तधा ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the golden post of his sacrifice, on its golden ring, six thousand gods and gandharvas danced in seven troupes."}},{"n":69,"text":"अवादयत्तत्र वीणां मध्ये विश्वावसुः स्वयम् ।\nसर्वभूतान्यमन्यन्त मम वादयतीत्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among them Vishvavasu himself played the lute, and all beings thought he was playing for them."}},{"n":70,"text":"एतद्राज्ञो दिलीपस्य राजानो नानुचक्रिरे ।\nयत्स्त्रियो हेमसंपन्नाः पथि मत्ताः स्म शेरते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Other kings did not imitate this deed of King Dilipa, that women rich in gold lay drunk on the road."}},{"n":71,"text":"राजानमुग्रधन्वानं दिलीपं सत्यवादिनम् ।\nयेऽपश्यन्सुमहात्मानं तेऽपि स्वर्गजितो नराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even those men who saw the truthful king Dilipa, great-souled, with his terrible bow, conquered heaven."}},{"n":72,"text":"त्रयः शब्दा न जीर्यन्ते दिलीपस्य निवेशने ।\nस्वाध्यायघोषो ज्याघोषो दीयतामिति चैव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Three sounds never ceased in Dilipa's house: the sound of Vedic study, the twang of the bowstring, and the cry \"Let it be given!\""}},{"n":73,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son."}},{"n":74,"text":"मान्धातारं यौवनाश्वं मृतं शुश्रुम सृञ्जय ।\nयं देवा मरुतो गर्भं पितुः पार्श्वादपाहरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that Mandhata, son of Yuvanashva, also died, whom the gods and Maruts took from his father's side as an unborn child."}},{"n":75,"text":"संवृद्धो युवनाश्वस्य जठरे यो महात्मनः ।\nपृषदाज्योद्भवः श्रीमांस्त्रिलोकविजयी नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That king, who grew in the womb of great-souled Yuvanashva, was born from ghee and conquered the three worlds, splendid."}},{"n":76,"text":"यं दृष्ट्वा पितुरुत्सङ्गे शयानं देवरूपिणम् ।\nअन्योन्यमब्रुवन्देवाः कमयं धास्यतीति वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him lying in his father's lap, with the form of a god, the gods asked one another, \"Whom will he suckle?\""}},{"n":77,"text":"मामेव धास्यतीत्येवमिन्द्रो अभ्यवपद्यत ।\nमान्धातेति ततस्तस्य नाम चक्रे शतक्रतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He will suckle me,\" said Indra, and the hundred-sacrifice god named him Mandhata."}},{"n":78,"text":"ततस्तु पयसो धारां पुष्टिहेतोर्महात्मनः ।\nतस्यास्ये यौवनाश्वस्य पाणिरिन्द्रस्य चास्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, for the great one's nourishment, a stream of milk flowed from Indra's hand into the mouth of Yuvanashva's son."}},{"n":79,"text":"तं पिबन्पाणिमिन्द्रस्य समामह्ना व्यवर्धत ।\nस आसीद्द्वादशसमो द्वादशाहेन पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drinking from Indra's hand, in a day he grew as much as a normal child grows in a year; in twelve days, O king, he was like a youth of twelve."}},{"n":80,"text":"तमियं पृथिवी सर्वा एकाह्ना समपद्यत ।\nधर्मात्मानं महात्मानं शूरमिन्द्रसमं युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"In one day the whole earth came under the sway of that righteous, great-souled hero, equal to Indra in battle."}},{"n":81,"text":"य आङ्गारं हि नृपतिं मरुत्तमसितं गयम् ।\nअङ्गं बृहद्रथं चैव मान्धाता समरेऽजयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mandhata defeated in battle King Angara, Marutta, Asita, Gaya and Anga Brihadratha."}},{"n":82,"text":"यौवनाश्वो यदाङ्गारं समरे समयोधयत् ।\nविस्फारैर्धनुषो देवा द्यौरभेदीति मेनिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Yuvanashva's son fought Angara in battle, the gods thought the sky was split by the twanging of his bow."}},{"n":83,"text":"यतः सूर्य उदेति स्म यत्र च प्रतितिष्ठति ।\nसर्वं तद्यौवनाश्वस्य मान्धातुः क्षेत्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wherever the sun rises and wherever it sets, all of it is called the domain of Mandhata, son of Yuvanashva."}},{"n":84,"text":"अश्वमेधशतेनेष्ट्वा राजसूयशतेन च ।\nअददाद्रोहितान्मत्स्यान्ब्राह्मणेभ्यो महीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After sacrificing with a hundred horse sacrifices and a hundred royal consecrations, that lord of the earth gave brahmins red fish."}},{"n":85,"text":"हैरण्यान्योजनोत्सेधानायतान्दशयोजनम् ।\nअतिरिक्तान्द्विजातिभ्यो व्यभजन्नितरे जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those golden fish, a yojana high and ten yojanas long, were so many that others divided the surplus among the brahmins."}},{"n":86,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son."}},{"n":87,"text":"ययातिं नाहुषं चैव मृतं शुश्रुम सृञ्जय ।\nय इमां पृथिवीं सर्वां विजित्य सहसागराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that Yayati, son of Nahusha, also died, who conquered this whole earth with its oceans."}},{"n":88,"text":"शम्यापातेनाभ्यतीयाद्वेदीभिश्चित्रयन्नृप ।\nईजानः क्रतुभिः पुण्यैः पर्यगच्छद्वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, he adorned the land with altars as far as a thrown yoke-pin would fly, and by his holy sacrifices he traversed the earth."}},{"n":89,"text":"इष्ट्वा क्रतुसहस्रेण वाजिमेधशतेन च ।\nतर्पयामास देवेन्द्रं त्रिभिः काञ्चनपर्वतैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having sacrificed with a thousand rites and a hundred horse sacrifices, he gratified Indra with three golden mountains."}},{"n":90,"text":"व्यूढे देवासुरे युद्धे हत्वा दैतेयदानवान् ।\nव्यभजत्पृथिवीं कृत्स्नां ययातिर्नहुषात्मजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the battle of gods and asuras was joined, Yayati, son of Nahusha, killed the Daityas and Danavas and divided the whole earth."}},{"n":91,"text":"अन्तेषु पुत्रान्निक्षिप्य यदुद्रुह्युपुरोगमान् ।\nपूरुं राज्येऽभिषिच्य स्वे सदारः प्रस्थितो वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Placing his sons, Yadu, Druhyu and the others, at the borders, he installed Puru in his kingdom and set out for the forest with his wife."}},{"n":92,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son."}},{"n":93,"text":"अम्बरीषं च नाभागं मृतं शुश्रुम सृञ्जय ।\nयं प्रजा वव्रिरे पुण्यं गोप्तारं नृपसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that Ambarisha, son of Nabhaga, also died, whom the people chose as their virtuous protector, best of kings."}},{"n":94,"text":"यः सहस्रं सहस्राणां राज्ञामयुत याजिनाम् ।\nईजानो वितते यज्ञे ब्राह्मणेभ्यः समाहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At his wide-spread sacrifice he gave to the brahmins, with focused mind, a thousand times a thousand kings who performed ten thousand sacrifices."}},{"n":95,"text":"नैतत्पूर्वे जनाश्चक्रुर्न करिष्यन्ति चापरे ।\nइत्यम्बरीषं नाभागमन्वमोदन्त दक्षिणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Neither those before nor those after will do this,\" said the fees in praise of Ambarisha, son of Nabhaga."}},{"n":96,"text":"शतं राजसहस्राणि शतं राजशतानि च ।\nसर्वेऽश्वमेधैरीजानास्तेऽभ्ययुर्दक्षिणायनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A hundred thousand kings and a hundred hundred more, all having performed horse sacrifices, went to the southern path."}},{"n":97,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son."}},{"n":98,"text":"शशबिन्दुं चैत्ररथं मृतं शुश्रुम सृञ्जय ।\nयस्य भार्यासहस्राणां शतमासीन्महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that Shashabindu, son of Chitraratha, also died, the great soul who had a hundred thousand wives."}},{"n":99,"text":"सहस्रं तु सहस्राणां यस्यासञ्शाशबिन्दवः ।\nहिरण्यकवचाः सर्वे सर्वे चोत्तमधन्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A thousand times a thousand sons were born to him, the Shashabindus, all in golden armor and all superb archers."}},{"n":100,"text":"शतं कन्या राजपुत्रमेकैकं पृष्ठतोऽन्वयुः ।\nकन्यां कन्यां शतं नागा नागं नागं शतं रथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A hundred maidens followed each prince, a hundred elephants each maiden, a hundred chariots each elephant."}},{"n":101,"text":"रथं रथं शतं चाश्वा देशजा हेममालिनः ।\nअश्वमश्वं शतं गावो गां गां तद्वदजाविकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A hundred horses of good breed with golden garlands followed each chariot, a hundred cows each horse, and as many goats and sheep each cow."}},{"n":102,"text":"एतद्धनमपर्यन्तमश्वमेधे महामखे ।\nशशबिन्दुर्महाराज ब्राह्मणेभ्यः समादिशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, Shashabindu assigned all this endless wealth to the brahmins at his great horse sacrifice."}},{"n":103,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son."}},{"n":104,"text":"गयमामूर्तरयसं मृतं शुश्रुम सृञ्जय ।\nयः स वर्षशतं राजा हुतशिष्टाशनोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that Gaya, of swift and embodied energy, also died, who for a hundred years lived on what remained of the offerings."}},{"n":105,"text":"यस्मै वह्निर्वरान्प्रादात्ततो वव्रे वरान्गयः ।\nददतो मेऽक्षया चास्तु धर्मे श्रद्धा च वर्धताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Agni gave him boons, Gaya chose: \"May my giving never run out, may my faith in dharma grow.\""}},{"n":106,"text":"मनो मे रमतां सत्ये त्वत्प्रसादाद्धुताशन ।\nलेभे च कामांस्तान्सर्वान्पावकादिति नः श्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let my mind delight in truth, by your grace, Eater of oblations.\" We have heard that he obtained all those wishes from Agni."}},{"n":107,"text":"दर्शेन पौर्णमासेन चातुर्मास्यैः पुनः पुनः ।\nअयजत्स महातेजाः सहस्रं परिवत्सरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That radiant king sacrificed with the new-moon, full-moon and four-monthly rites again and again for a thousand years."}},{"n":108,"text":"शतं गवां सहस्राणि शतमश्वशतानि च ।\nउत्थायोत्थाय वै प्रादात्सहस्रं परिवत्सरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He rose each time and gave a hundred thousand cows and a hundred hundred horses, for a thousand years."}},{"n":109,"text":"तर्पयामास सोमेन देवान्वित्तैर्द्विजानपि ।\nपितॄन्स्वधाभिः कामैश्च स्त्रियः स्वाः पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bull among men, he gratified the gods with soma, the brahmins with wealth, the ancestors with offerings, and his wives with their desires."}},{"n":110,"text":"सौवर्णां पृथिवीं कृत्वा दशव्यामां द्विरायताम् ।\nदक्षिणामददद्राजा वाजिमेधमहामखे ॥","meaning":{"en":"At his great horse sacrifice the king made a golden earth, ten vyamas wide and twice as long, and gave it as the fee."}},{"n":111,"text":"यावत्यः सिकता राजन्गङ्गायाः पुरुषर्षभ ।\nतावतीरेव गाः प्रादादामूर्तरयसो गयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, bull among men, as many grains of sand as lie in the Ganga, that many cows Gaya of swift energy gave."}},{"n":112,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son."}},{"n":113,"text":"रन्तिदेवं च साङ्कृत्यं मृतं शुश्रुम सृञ्जय ।\nसम्यगाराध्य यः शक्रं वरं लेभे महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that Rantideva Sankritya also died, the greatly famed who won a boon after properly worshiping Indra."}},{"n":114,"text":"अन्नं च नो बहु भवेदतिथींश्च लभेमहि ।\nश्रद्धा च नो मा व्यगमन्मा च याचिष्म कंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"May we have plenty of food, may we find guests, may our faith never leave us, and may we never beg from anyone.\""}},{"n":115,"text":"उपातिष्ठन्त पशवः स्वयं तं संशितव्रतम् ।\nग्राम्यारण्या महात्मानं रन्तिदेवं यशस्विनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Domestic and wild animals came of themselves to the great, famous Rantideva, firm in his vows."}},{"n":116,"text":"महानदी चर्मराशेरुत्क्लेदात्सुस्रुवे यतः ।\nततश्चर्मण्वतीत्येवं विख्याता सा महानदी ॥","meaning":{"en":"From the oozing of heaps of hides, a great river flowed, and so that great river became known as Charmanvati."}},{"n":117,"text":"ब्राह्मणेभ्यो ददौ निष्कान्सदसि प्रतते नृपः ।\nतुभ्यं तुभ्यं निष्कमिति यत्राक्रोशन्ति वै द्विजाः ।\nसहस्रं तुभ्यमित्युक्त्वा ब्राह्मणान्स्म प्रपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"In his crowded hall the king gave brahmins gold coins, and the brahmins there cried out, \"To you, to you the coin!\" and he approached them saying, \"A thousand to you.\""}},{"n":118,"text":"अन्वाहार्योपकरणं द्रव्योपकरणं च यत् ।\nघटाः स्थाल्यः कटाहाश्च पात्र्यश्च पिठरा अपि ।\nन तत्किंचिदसौवर्णं रन्तिदेवस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever he used for his utensils and implements, pots, pans, cauldrons, dishes and jars, nothing of wise Rantideva's was not of gold."}},{"n":119,"text":"साङ्कृते रन्तिदेवस्य यां रात्रिमवसद्गृहे ।\nआलभ्यन्त शतं गावः सहस्राणि च विंशतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the night that guests stayed in Rantideva's house, a hundred cows and twenty thousand more were sacrificed."}},{"n":120,"text":"तत्र स्म सूदाः क्रोशन्ति सुमृष्टमणिकुण्डलाः ।\nसूपभूयिष्ठमश्नीध्वं नाद्य मांसं यथा पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the cooks, with polished jewelled earrings, would call out, \"Eat plenty of soup; there is not as much meat today as before.\""}},{"n":121,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son."}},{"n":122,"text":"सगरं च महात्मानं मृतं शुश्रुम सृञ्जय ।\nऐक्ष्वाकं पुरुषव्याघ्रमतिमानुषविक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that great-souled Sagara also died, the Ikshvaku, tiger among men, of superhuman valor."}},{"n":123,"text":"षष्टिः पुत्रसहस्राणि यं यान्तं पृष्ठतोऽन्वयुः ।\nनक्षत्रराजं वर्षान्ते व्यभ्रे ज्योतिर्गणा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sixty thousand sons followed him as he went, like stars attending the king of the stars in a cloudless sky at the end of the rains."}},{"n":124,"text":"एकच्छत्रा मही यस्य प्रणता ह्यभवत्पुरा ।\nयोऽश्वमेधसहस्रेण तर्पयामास देवताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the past the whole earth bowed under one umbrella to him, and he gratified the gods with a thousand horse sacrifices."}},{"n":125,"text":"यः प्रादात्काञ्चनस्तम्भं प्रासादं सर्वकाञ्चनम् ।\nपूर्णं पद्मदलाक्षीणां स्त्रीणां शयनसंकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He gave a palace with golden pillars, all of gold, filled with lotus-eyed women and crowded with couches."}},{"n":126,"text":"द्विजातिभ्योऽनुरूपेभ्यः कामानुच्चावचांस्तथा ।\nयस्यादेशेन तद्वित्तं व्यभजन्त द्विजातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At his command the brahmins divided that wealth among themselves, giving suitable brahmins desires of every kind."}},{"n":127,"text":"खानयामास यः कोपात्पृथिवीं सागराङ्किताम् ।\nयस्य नाम्ना समुद्रश्च सागरत्वमुपागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In anger he had the earth, marked by oceans, dug out, and through his name the ocean came to be called a sagara."}},{"n":128,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son."}},{"n":129,"text":"राजानं च पृथुं वैन्यं मृतं शुश्रुम सृञ्जय ।\nयमभ्यषिञ्चन्संभूय महारण्ये महर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, we have heard that King Prithu, son of Vena, also died, whom the great sages gathered together in the great forest and consecrated."}},{"n":130,"text":"प्रथयिष्यति वै लोकान्पृथुरित्येव शब्दितः ।\nक्षताच्च नस्त्रायतीति स तस्मात्क्षत्रियः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He will make the worlds widely known, being called Prithu, and he saves us from harm,\" so he is remembered as a kshatriya."}},{"n":131,"text":"पृथुं वैन्यं प्रजा दृष्ट्वा रक्ताः स्मेति यदब्रुवन् ।\nततो राजेति नामास्य अनुरागादजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the people saw Prithu, Vena's son, they said, \"We are delighted\"; so from their affection the name \"king\" arose for him."}},{"n":132,"text":"अकृष्टपच्या पृथिवी पुटके पुटके मधु ।\nसर्वा द्रोणदुघा गावो वैन्यस्यासन्प्रशासतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Vena's son ruled, the earth bore crops unploughed, honey filled every leaf-cup, and all cows gave a full measure of milk."}},{"n":133,"text":"अरोगाः सर्वसिद्धार्था मनुष्या अकुतोभयाः ।\nयथाभिकाममवसन्क्षेत्रेषु च गृहेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men were free of disease, all their aims fulfilled and fearless, and they lived as they wished in fields and in houses."}},{"n":134,"text":"आपः संस्तम्भिरे यस्य समुद्रस्य यियासतः ।\nसरितश्चानुदीर्यन्त ध्वजसङ्गश्च नाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he wished to cross the ocean the waters stood firm, rivers rose up, and his banner was never obstructed."}},{"n":135,"text":"हैरण्यांस्त्रिनलोत्सेधान्पर्वतानेकविंशतिम् ।\nब्राह्मणेभ्यो ददौ राजा योऽश्वमेधे महामखे ॥","meaning":{"en":"At his great horse sacrifice the king gave the brahmins twenty-one golden mountains, each three nalas high."}},{"n":136,"text":"स चेन्ममार सृञ्जय चतुर्भद्रतरस्त्वया ।\nपुत्रात्पुण्यतरश्चैव मा पुत्रमनुतप्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya, if he died, who was four times better than you and more virtuous than your son, do not grieve for your son."}},{"n":137,"text":"किं वै तूष्णीं ध्यायसि सृञ्जय त्वं\nन मे राजन्वाचमिमां शृणोषि ।\nन चेन्मोघं विप्रलप्तं मयेदं\nपथ्यं मुमूर्षोरिव सम्यगुक्तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Why do you sit silent in thought, Srinjaya? King, do you not hear these words of mine? I hope my speech, like good counsel to a dying man, was not spoken in vain."}},{"text":"सृञ्जय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Srinjaya said:"}},{"n":138,"text":"शृणोमि ते नारद वाचमेतां\nविचित्रार्थां स्रजमिव पुण्यगन्धाम् ।\nराजर्षीणां पुण्यकृतां महात्मनां\nकीर्त्या युक्तां शोकनिर्णाशनार्थम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Narada, I hear your words, of varied meaning like a garland of sacred fragrance, joined with the glory of virtuous, great-souled royal sages, and meant to destroy grief."}},{"n":139,"text":"न ते मोघं विप्रलप्तं महर्षे\nदृष्ट्वैव त्वां नारदाहं विशोकः ।\nशुश्रूषे ते वचनं ब्रह्मवादि-\nन्न ते तृप्याम्यमृतस्येव पानात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great sage, your speech was not spoken in vain; at the mere sight of you, Narada, I am free of sorrow. I wish to hear you, teller of Brahman, and like drinking nectar I am never satisfied."}},{"n":140,"text":"अमोघदर्शिन्मम चेत्प्रसादं\nसुताघदग्धस्य विभो प्रकुर्याः ।\nमृतस्य संजीवनमद्य मे स्या-\nत्तव प्रसादात्सुतसंगमश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seer whose vision is never fruitless, if you would show me grace, scorched as I am by my son's misfortune, then today, lord, let there be life for my dead son and reunion with him by your favor."}},{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":141,"text":"यस्ते पुत्रो दयितोऽयं वियातः\nस्वर्णष्ठीवी यमदात्पर्वतस्ते ।\nपुनस्ते तं पुत्रमहं ददामि\nहिरण्यनाभं वर्षसहस्रिणं च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your beloved son who has died, whom the mountain Parvata gave you, he of the golden spit, I give back to you, with the name Hiranyanabha, to live a thousand years."}}]}]}